The '''1994 Wyoming gubernatorial election''' took place on November 8, 1994. Incumbent Democratic Governor [[Mike Sullivan (governor)|Mike Sullivan]] was unable to seek a third term because of newly imposed term limits, and instead [[1994 United States Senate election in Wyoming|ran for the U.S. Senate]]. State Senate President [[Jim Geringer]] won the Republican primary and faced Secretary of State [[Kathy Karpan]], the Democratic nominee, in the general election. Aided by the [[1994 United States elections|nationwide Republican wave]], Geringer defeated Karpan in a landslide, marking the first time since Governor [[Stanley Hathaway]]'s re-election in [[1970 Wyoming gubernatorial election|1970]] that a Republican won a gubernatorial election in Wyoming.

